---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Link from '../../components/Link.astro';
---

<Layout title="Cookie Policy — Motiva Hub" description="Which cookies Motiva Hub uses, what each category does, how consent is collected through Google Privacy & messaging, and how to change your choices." image="/images/youssef-raihane.jpg" lang="en">
  <article class="article-body container">
    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="card-meta">LEGAL</p>
        <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="card-date">Last updated: October 30, 2026</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Cookies Are</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files stored by your browser when you visit a site. They let a site remember a choice or measure how its pages are used. This policy covers cookies and similar technologies (local storage, pixels) on the-motivahub.com, in both the English and French versions.</p>

      <h2>The Categories We Use</h2>
      <h3>1. Strictly necessary</h3>
      <p>These keep the site working: page delivery, security, form submission and your language choice. Your language preference and the state of the interactive tools (habit tracker, cold shower tracker) are stored locally in your browser, not in advertising cookies. Necessary storage is used without consent because the site cannot function without it.</p>

      <h3>2. Analytics</h3>
      <p>Google Analytics 4 measures how pages are read: page views, approximate country, device type and navigation paths. These cookies are set only after you consent. Before consent, analytics runs in restricted mode (Consent Mode v2: <code>analytics_storage</code> denied) and does not read or write analytics cookies.</p>

      <h3>3. Advertising</h3>
      <p>Google AdSense serves the advertisements on article pages. Advertising cookies are set only after you consent to advertising storage. Before consent, the ad tag runs in restricted mode (<code>ad_storage</code>, <code>ad_user_data</code> and <code>ad_personalization</code> denied), which means no personalised advertising cookies are set.</p>

      <h2>How Consent Is Collected</h2>
      <p>Consent is collected through <strong>Google Privacy &amp; messaging</strong> (Google's consent management platform, also called Funding Choices), which shows a message when you first visit from a region that requires it. You choose per purpose, and the choice is remembered for that browser.</p>
      <p>You can change or withdraw your choice at any time with the <a href="#consent" data-consent-revoke onclick="var done=false;try{if(window.googlefc&&googlefc.showRevocationMessage){googlefc.showRevocationMessage();done=true;}}catch(e){}if(!done){window.location.href='/privacy/';}return false;">Manage consent</a> control, also available in the footer of every page. Withdrawal applies from that moment; it does not affect processing that happened before it.</p>

      <h2>Third-Party Cookies</h2>
      <p>When you consent, the following third parties may set cookies:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (<code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code>) — audience measurement.</li>
        <li><strong>Google AdSense</strong> (<code>__gads</code>, <code>__gpi</code>) — ad delivery, frequency capping and fraud prevention.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Privacy &amp; messaging</strong> — your consent choices.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each of these is described in Google's own <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies" rel="noopener nofollow" target="_blank">cookie documentation</a>. We do not sell personal data, and we do not run any other advertising network.</p>

      <h2>How Long Cookies Last</h2>
      <p>Session cookies disappear when you close the browser. Persistent cookies have an expiry set by their provider — analytics and advertising cookies typically last up to 13 months. You can delete them at any time from your browser settings.</p>

      <h2>Managing Cookies in Your Browser</h2>
      <p>Every major browser lets you see, block and delete cookies, and browse in private mode. Blocking necessary storage may break parts of the site; blocking advertising cookies does not remove the ads, it only makes them non-personalised. See your browser's help pages for the exact steps.</p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>If we add a service that sets cookies, this page is updated and the date at the top changes.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about cookies or consent? Write to <a href="mailto:contact@the-motivahub.com">contact@the-motivahub.com</a>, or read the <Link href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</Link> for the wider picture.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
